  "requirements_proven": [
    "One actual accepted Message reply is withheld. The uncertain browser peer times out, closes and explicitly reconnects; recovery reads the original completed Operation without another mutation. Proxy counts one new Message command, one exact original ID; SQL requires one Message, one original send Operation/record and exactly one journal fact for each of two original enrolled recipients.",
    "An established WSS socket is forcibly terminated. While upgrades are refused and preferred WT is blackholed, bounded reconnect fails; no implicit reconnect runs. Restoring WSS permits explicit original-status recovery.",
    "An established authenticated WT path first observes the original completed Operation. UDP relay then drops actual packets: a bounded read expires and retires the old lifetime once. Explicit reconnect selects WSS with preferred-transport-timeout, observes the same Operation, then restores WT explicitly after UDP resumes.",
    "A separately issued, same-actor/Device scoped credential successfully authenticates and reads the original status before its real 45-second expiry. After the clock boundary reads fail and reconnect is refused during authentication; valid current enrollment restores access.",
    "A second independently issued/bound scoped credential reads successfully, is revoked through the protected production HTTP provisioning endpoint, then fails current reads and authentication. Restoring valid authority recovers the same original status.",
    "Browser, Node, proxy, service and physical routes/slots join or retire on every passing lane. Existing unready transition parity oracle remains separate and passes."
  ],
